.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt USBROLE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm usbrole
.Nd a USB port as a device or a host, as Type-C says
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl 1
.Nm
.Fl d
.Nm
.Op Fl t Ar seconds
.Cm host | device | auto
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A machine whose one USB port is both its network to the computer at the
other end of the cable and the place a keyboard is plugged in has to
decide which the port is.
.Nm
decides it from what the PMIC's Type-C block says is at the other end
.Pq Va minix.pmic.typec :
a sink \(em an OTG adapter, a device \(em makes the port a host; anything
else, including no answer, leaves it a device.
.Pp
The device role is the network driver named by the boot parameter
.Va netdrv
(label
.Ar netdrv Ns _0 )
with the address
.Va netaddr ;
the host role is
.Nm xhci
(label
.Li usbd ) ,
.Nm usb_hub ,
.Nm usb_kbd
and
.Nm usb_mouse .
The one is taken down before the other comes up: they drive the same
controller.
.Pp
Without arguments
.Nm
prints the role, the policy, the Type-C state and where VBUS comes from.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl 1
Decide once and bring that role up; the
.Pa /etc/rc
of the machine does this before it starts
.Nm sshd .
.It Fl d
Follow Type-C from now on, in the background; a change has to be seen
twice, a second apart, before anything moves.
.It Oo Fl t Ar seconds Oc Cm host | device | auto
Ask the daemon for a role \(em for that many seconds, or until asked
again.
.Cm auto
follows Type-C again.
.El
.Pp
The boot parameter
.Va usbrole
is the policy:
.Cm auto
(the default),
.Cm device
(nothing is done) or
.Cm host .
With
.Cm auto
the PMIC is told to let the port be a source
.Pq Va minix.pmic.otg Ns = Ns Cm auto ,
without which Type-C never sees a sink at all.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/run/usbrole.want -compact
.It Pa /var/run/usbrole.role
the role that is up
.It Pa /var/run/usbrole.want
the role asked for, and until when
.It Pa /var/run/usbrole.pid
the daemon
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr minix-service 8 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh BUGS
Try.SNK is not done: with a dual-role partner at the other end (a
computer's USB-C port) which end becomes the source is a matter of
timing.
